// SPEC qa.md appendix section 1: "`U<N>`/`S<N>`/`Unsigned`/`Signed`/`Bool`/`String`/`Clock`/`Reset` are RESERVED type
// words: they cannot be declared as variable/port/parameter/field names; a variable with that spelling must be
// backticked". Section 7: "Reserved `U<N>`/`S<N>` = `U`/`S` followed by ANY digit string (U0, U1333, U99999999),
// reserved EVERYWHERE including after `.` (fields/attributes)."
// Rule: `S99999999` (any digit string) is a reserved type word, not a name.
const S99999999 = 1  // locate_error_here
